<!--Post: 7566--><!--Time: 1108581119-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7566"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Neechi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Neechi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 11:11 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I just received a breaking news e-mail from KWCH Channel 12 stating that their sister station KSAS Fox Channel 24, received a suspicious mailing that they think may be from BTK.  Here&#39;s the text of the e-mail. &#40;I couldn&#39;t find it on their website to include a link&#41; <BR> <BR>KWCH 12 Eyewitness News Breaking News <BR>Possible BTK Package <BR> <BR>Wichita police are investigating a possible new communication from BTK-- a mailing to KSAS-TV Wednesday morning. Two employees from Fox Kansas going through the mail discovered it, which contains items that may be from BTK. <BR> <BR>At police request, Eyewitness News is not revealing the contents. Workers called police, who took it as evidence. Investigators are looking over the mailing to determine whether it is from BTK.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7566-->
<!--Post: 7570--><!--Time: 1108582147-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7570"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:BTK_Catcher@cox.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Catcher<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Catcher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 11:29 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Interesting, he has never sent direct communication to them before, correct?  I hope once verified, they will disclose more info.  We&#39;re tired of the pleas for help, with no guiding light! <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7570-->
<!--Post: 7574--><!--Time: 1108582988-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7574"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tadpole<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tadpole<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 11:43 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I wonder if &#34;FOX&#34; &#40;as in Nancy&#41; has anything to do with it. More game playing IMO.  <BR> <BR>I was just thinking last night, if this stuff is from BTK and he has had these momentos all these years, he would have handled them at one time or another most likely without gloves on, leaving prints.  I understand that LE has DNA and I would almost bet on it that they have found some &#40;at least&#41; partial prints that would be usable.  <BR> <BR>And while I am spouting off...that Det. F. Cummins, I understand his sense of privacy for his family, but I would think that he would be more interested in proving that he is NOT the perp than protecting his family. IMO it sound more like he has something to hide. That is only my opinion. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7574-->
<!--Post: 7588--><!--Time: 1108590151-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7588"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:newmilleniumwriter@yahoo.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tippy<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tippy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 1:42 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I just heard that blurb, also.  How strange.  Do you think BTK is tired of KAKE not releasing his info?   <BR> <BR>I can&#39;t quite put my finger on it - but something sure smells fishy about all communications lately. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7588-->
<!--Post: 7593--><!--Time: 1108591691-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7593"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:vscantu1@msn.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vscantu<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vscantu<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 2:08 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->TIPPY wrote: &#34;I can&#39;t quite put my finger on it - but something sure smells fishy about all communications lately.&#34; <BR> <BR>TIPPY: EVERYTHING about this case &#34;smells fishy&#34;- and has for 31 years. Get used to it.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7593-->
<!--Post: 7595--><!--Time: 1108593081-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7595"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Icyou<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Icyou<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 2:31 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Fox is a more liberal network, maybe he does think they&#39;ll give out more info.  I also agreee it could be a wordplay on Nancy Fox.  Who knows?  Doesn&#39;t it piss you off how he intrigues us so? <BR> <BR>a little sidenote....I saw a commercial on KAKE this morning about the huge jumps in their ratings.  Yeah, no s&#42;&#42;&#42;!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7595-->
<!--Post: 7603--><!--Time: 1108596127-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7603"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lorenap<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lorenap<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 3:22 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->KWCH channel 12 and Fox news are sister staions here in Wichita. The package was delivered by mail to the KSAS Fox studios on N. West Street. It looked liked a smaller sized package in a brown postal type envelope. It had several stamps on it and that is one of the things that caught the eye of the worker who found it. The postcard said something to the effect of KAKE is a good station and all but he &#40;btk&#41; thought they were being singled out because of all the attention etc.... I will try to get a link if someone does not already have one up.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7603-->
<!--Post: 7604--><!--Time: 1108596373-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7604"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lorenap<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lorenap<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 3:26 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Sorry no video up yet. just earlier posted transcript. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7604-->
<!--Post: 7609--><!--Time: 1108599907-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7609"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Essevi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Essevi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 4:25 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Communication 11? What happened to 10? <BR> <BR>Reports say there was a necklace, but not Nancy Fox&#39;s.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7609-->
<!--Post: 7612--><!--Time: 1108601282-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7612"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 4:48 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><a href="http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/10916990.htm" target=_top>http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/10916990.htm</a> <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.kake.com/news/headlines/1272122.html" target=_top>http://www.kake.com/news/headlines/1272122.html</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7612-->
<!--Post: 7623--><!--Time: 1108610060-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7623"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Kansasgirl<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Kansasgirl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 7:14 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It said it was Communication #11. Did I miss something. The police have admitted getting one other package, although they are not saying what or where. That still leaves one more since the cereal boxes. FOX news said that the package contained a letter, picture, and jewelry. The WPD is saying that all indications show that the letter is real. I noticed that at the bottom of the card it said something to the effect of &#34;From this point forward I will use the following code in order to verify the letters.&#34; Of course it was blacked out. Maybe they will put the video up soon so that we can take a better look at the package.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7623-->
<!--Post: 7624--><!--Time: 1108610406-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7624"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Kansasgirl<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Kansasgirl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 7:20 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Sorry, I forgot about the HAPP KAKEMAN Postcard &#40;#9&#41;. Maybe the rumor about the pop tart box was more than a rumor??<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7624-->
<!--Post: 7640--><!--Time: 1108619607-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7640"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:hkenley@san.rr.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Chiefron<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Chiefron<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 9:53 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Here is a chronology of what we know about his communications or have been told by WPD and KAKE. This should explain the numbering. <BR> <BR>First and foremost. From what BTK says in Communication 11, we know that HAPP KAKEMANN post card was not # 9, but in fact had to be #10. <BR> <BR>Why? BTK says &#34;9 was KAKE message asking about 7 and 8&#34;.  <BR> <BR>HAPP KAKEMAN postcard from February 2, 2005 did not ask about 7 and 8. Rather it said &#34;Thank you for your quick response on 7 and 8&#34;. The Janurary 27, 2005 postcard to KAKE did, however, ask about both 7 and 8, and told them where to find both. <BR> <BR>So, if the February 16 letter to KSAS is #11 as it clearly states it is, and the Janruary 27 is # 9, as he clearly states in 11, then the February 2 postcard has to be 10.  <BR> <BR>In 11, BTK says #8 was 2nd Cereal Box, that leads us to assume #7 was also a Cereal Box, although WPD has not confirmed that. <BR> <BR>No missing communication. Sorry scavenger hunters. <BR> <BR>Here is the best list I can come up with. <BR> <BR>1&#41; Wichita Eagle receives Wegerle License. <BR>2&#41; KAKE receives chapter list. <BR>3&#41; WPD receives OTERO letter <BR>4&#41; Letter discovered at library <BR>5&#41; UPS drop <BR>6&#41; Murdock Park <BR>7&#41; Presumably 1st Cereal Box <BR>8&#41; 2nd Cereal Box  <BR>9&#41; Post card to KAKE asking about 7 and 8 <BR>10&#41; Happ Kakemann post card to KAKE <BR>11&#41; Letter to KSAS <BR> <BR>A couple things of note. The baby photo to KSN is excluded. BTK has never talked about the photo, there was no real reason to ever believe it was a communication from him except timing. I think it is safe to say, the baby photo is not from BTK based on his own numbering system. <BR> <BR>The same goes for the letters from California, but most have discounted those since the beginning. <BR> <BR>I hope this makes sense, I am making very few assumptions and absolutely none about the numbering from 7 thru 11. I am using BTKs own words from 11. <BR> <BR>Ron<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7640-->
<!--Post: 7641--><!--Time: 1108620323-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7641"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Stormy74<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Stormy74<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 10:05 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thank you Ron for that post. Helped me clear up several things since I am new here. I will have to read more about how the baby pic came into play. But that is for another thread!  <BR> <BR>Thanks, <BR>Stormy<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7641-->
<!--Post: 7644--><!--Time: 1108620823-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7644"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 10:13 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Nice work, Ron, thanks. Agree with you about the baby picture.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7644-->
<!--Post: 7647--><!--Time: 1108623502-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7647"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 10:58 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->As far as I know that January message was marked as Communication #8 ITSELF and told where to get the latest drop, and then asked if it had found #7.   <BR> <BR>More likely that either there&#39;s another message we don&#39;t know about, or the package that #8 directed the police to had a #9 inside it.  Then Happ Kappman was #10, and here we have #11<!--/Text--></td></tr>
