<!--Post: 7698--><!--Time: 1108658945-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7698"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:hkenley@san.rr.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Chiefron<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Chiefron<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 8:49 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Kansasgirl, <BR> <BR>This is what confuses me the most.  <BR> <BR>BTK clearly states the order of communications but the local media disputes it. I don&#39;t really get it. They keep insisting that HAPP KAKEMANN is #9 but they have never released a photo of the card without redacting the portion that tells us what communication it is. Nor have they released one of the S. Killet communication without the communication number redacted. Why?  <BR> <BR>The other question would be, is there something missing from the latest letter? It tells us what 7 8 and 9 were, clearly contradicting what local media is saying even though the info on 7 is redacted. But it makes no mention of 10, unless it is on the back of that page and they just choose not to show it. <BR> <BR>My point here is, at least in the area of his communication numbers BTK has been more honest than either KAKE or WPD, why should I believe what they are saying now? <BR> <BR>Ron<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7698-->
