<!--Post: 7734--><!--Time: 1108668175-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7734"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:hkenley@san.rr.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Chiefron<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Chiefron<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 11:22 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Emberage, <BR> <BR>The puzzles were received in the same multi page letter to KAKE in May or 2004, communication #2 if our list is correct. So the Chapter list and the puzzles arrived together. There is no telling whether more puzzles were included either. The top of each page of the puzzle is the title Chapter 8.  <BR> <BR>His communications are referencing different chapters, however we only have puzzles for chapter 8. He also is not going in order if we are to believe WPD.  <BR> <BR>Communication 9 &#40;by BTK&#39;s count&#41; references Chapter 9 &#34;Hits&#34; however all the information pertaining to his C9 ref is redacted on the released photos. <BR> <BR>Communication 11 references Chapter 4 &#34;Fetishes&#34; but again, the text leading up to the reference is redacted. <BR> <BR>Based on the information we have, I have to believe that puzzles exist for all of his chapters and not just chapter 8. He mentions something about them having received and understood something. It is obvious he follows the case and knows that they received the Chapter 8 puzzle and understand some of it. I have to assume he is asking if they have received and or understand the other puzzles that we have not been given a chance to see. <BR> <BR>Ron<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7734-->
<!--Post: 7737--><!--Time: 1108669567-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7737"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:hkenley@san.rr.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Chiefron<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Chiefron<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 11:46 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Just wanted to repost this with as much detail for each drop. <BR> <BR>1&#41; 3/19/2004 Wichita Eagle receives a letter from Bill Thomas Killman. It contained a single sheet of paper with a photo copy of Vicki Wegerle&#39;s License and 3 photos of her body in different positions.  <BR> <BR>2&#41; 05/05/2005 KAKE receives chapter list, the Chapter 8 puzzle and photocopy of 2 IDs and a badge.  <BR> <BR>3&#41; June 2004 WPD receives a letter from BTK. The contents of this letter have not been released to the public but is rumored to contain details fo the Otero murder. <BR> <BR>4&#41; 7/17/2004 A letter discovered at main branch of the Wichita library. Contents have not been released. <BR>  <BR>5&#41; 10/22/2004 A manilla envolope is found in a UPS drop box. The envelope reportedly contained pictures and names.  <BR> <BR>6&#41; 12/14/2004 A bag is discovered in Murdock Park. The bag contained Nancy Fox&#39;s license, and a copy of the chapter list among other things not released at the time.  <BR> <BR>7&#41; Week of Jan 08, 2005. Presumably 1st Cereal Box. Contents unknown, discovered with BTKs assistance from communication 9 on 1/26/2005 <BR> <BR>8&#41; Week of Jan 17, 2005. Post Toasties Cereal Box Presumably 2nd Cereal Box, discovered with BTK assistance from communication 9 on 1/25/2005. Box contained among other things, jewelry and a reference to Chapter 9. <BR>  <BR>9&#41; 1/25/2005 S. Killet Post card to KAKE telling them where to find Cereal Box 2 &#40;#8&#41;, and asking them if they had found Cereal Box 1 &#40;#7&#41; and giving its location as well. <BR> <BR>10&#41; 2/3/2005 Happ Kakemann post card to KAKE thanking them for quick response on 7 and 8 and offering condolences to Susan and Jeff. <BR>  <BR>11&#41; 2/15/2005 PJ Fox Letter to KSAS short summary of why he is communicating with them instead of KAKE, contains a new Code# for future verification of his communications with them. Makes reference to Chapter 4. Asks them if they have received and understand something. However those refs are redacted. <BR> <BR>Ron<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7737-->
<!--Post: 7740--><!--Time: 1108671083-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7740"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Surfietx<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Surfietx<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 12:11 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Check this out.. <BR> <BR><a href="http://forums.prospero.com/foxamw/messages/?msg=1616.1" target=_top>http://forums.prospero.com/foxamw/messages/?msg=16 16.1</a> <BR> <BR>Scroll down a bit to the P.S. section.  <BR> <BR>#7 is blacked out <BR>#8 was the 2nd cereal box - PT <BR>#9 was KAKE message asking about #7 and 8. <BR> <BR>So, you are right, Chief.   <BR> <BR>He seems very intent on making sure the numbers are right and correlate to the proper messages/drops.  Significant? <BR> <BR>Also I think the HAPP KAKEMANN referenced the fact that he was &#39;THE&#39; KAKEMANN, but not much longer as now he is communicating with someone other than KAKE.  Maybe the HAPP stood for happy?  I&#39;m not sure?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7740-->
<!--Post: 7762--><!--Time: 1108674804-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7762"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Msrusty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Msrusty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 1:13 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->In which of the drops was the baby pic included? I&#39;ve read both that it was from him and that it wasn&#39;t. Which is it, does anybody know for sure?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7762-->
<!--Post: 7766--><!--Time: 1108675835-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7766"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Neechi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Neechi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 1:30 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->No one from area LE have ever said that it is a confirmed communication from BTK.  There was some local media speculation, partially because a lot of people feel the baby picture resembles Shirley Vian.  But it has never been stated to be a &#34;true&#34; communication from BTK.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7766-->
<!--Post: 7773--><!--Time: 1108677408-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7773"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:hkenley@san.rr.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Chiefron<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Chiefron<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 1:56 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Msrusty, <BR> <BR>The baby picture was delivered on its own to KSN in April of 2004. It was sent anonymously. KSN believed it could be related to BTK only because of the timing. There is no evidence to suggest that it has anything to do with BTK and that is why I left it off the list. <BR> <BR>Ron<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7773-->
<!--Post: 7811--><!--Time: 1108688568-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7811"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Msrusty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Msrusty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 5:02 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thanks for the answer, Ron. That&#39;s what I thought too but since I&#39;m fairly new to the case I asked. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7811-->
<!--Post: 7821--><!--Time: 1108692783-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7821"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 6:13 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The &#34;BTK Story Chapter list&#34; is, originally based,on the &#34;Crime Library Chapter List&#34; <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.crimelibrary.com/serial_killers/unsolved/btk/index_1.html?sect=4" target=_top>http://www.crimelibrary.com/serial_killers/unsolve d/btk/index_1.html?sect=4</a> <BR> <BR>BTK has changed and keeps changing the chapter titles to fit the way he wants things to unfold and I would assume that the KAKE list is the accurate one to use for reference. <BR> <BR>The &#34;C.4. the start of BWs or EWs&#34; reference in the letter contained in the latest drop,could refer to drop #4 &#40;which has not been released to the public&#41;, or Chapter #4 Fantasy World or the original chapter name &#34;Different Worlds Collide&#34;.  <BR> <BR>&#34;Different Worlds Collide&#34; refers to the time that the public had become aware that a serial killer was definately active in Wichita, and specifically to the Nancy Fox murder and has a composite drawing of BTK showing him with dark skin and a moustache, and looking around 25 years old. <BR> <BR>This is also where the chapters start to be renamed. He has changed that Chapter To &#34;Fantasy World&#34;. <BR> <BR>Does anyone have any idea what the BW or EW &#40;letter in drop at FOX&#41; refers to? Black/Whites possibly, as in potographs? The Crime Library story also shows a B/W photo of Nancy Fox but if it is the same photo as the one showing the necklace, it is too small to be visible. <BR> <BR>Does anyone have any idea why BTK would refer back to this point in time, specifically, at this time. <BR> <BR>Is this just a reaffirmation from BTK that he is calling the shots &#40;as was suggested by one newscast&#41; by reminding us that he will write his story his own way?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7821-->
<!--Post: 7838--><!--Time: 1108706712-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7838"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Icyou<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Icyou<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 10:05 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Bmodule, <BR> <BR>Thank you!  I was getting annoyed that the news reports were trying to make it look like BTK had wirtten the chapters himself.  I wish they would have informed people that he was just modifying something that was already written.  Another way the public is being misinformed.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7838-->
<!--Post: 7846--><!--Time: 1108709682-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7846"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dsv<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dsv<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 10:54 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->IMO the portions of BTK&#39;s messages that are redacted are actually direct responses to LE in response to direct communctions to BTK from LE &#40;that LE has never made public&#41;. <BR> <BR>In other words, &#40;&#34;I got your message&#34;&#41;, &#40;&#34;I found your message in the LA Times&#34;&#41; or &#40;&#34;Not going to turn myself in yet&#34;&#41;  etc.  <BR> <BR>It wouldn&#39;t be unusual at all for LE to be communicating to BTK for example through the LA or New York times &#40;far removed from Wichita&#41;, since the FBI is involved. <BR> <BR>Obviously since LE has in the past and continues even now to withold information about this case tells me that BTK is communcated directly with LE and it&#39;s his answers that are redacted.   <BR> <BR>As a result he send messages to the news media to keep the public informed &#40;since LE wants to hide everything&#41;. This way at least some of his communications are made public because of KAKE. <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7846-->
<!--Post: 7891--><!--Time: 1108736875-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7891"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rev<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rev<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 18, 2005 - 6:27 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Bmodule: Most people have &#34;decided&#34; that on the FOX communication, it says &#39;C.4 The start of FWs&#39; meaning Fantasy World&#40;s&#41; which is Chapter 4 on his list. <BR> <BR>I thought it was EW when I first saw it, but I would agree with most others that it is FW.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7891-->
<!--Post: 7895--><!--Time: 1108739579-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7895"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 18, 2005 - 7:12 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I agree since we know that C4 chapter four fw in the crime Library is all about Nancy fox. Fantasy World We also believe that The M letter = 13 Chapter 13 More clues revealed.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7895-->
<!--Post: 7920--><!--Time: 1108747214-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7920"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Icyou<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Icyou<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 18, 2005 - 9:20 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Dsv, <BR> <BR>Yes, I would agree that he has communicated directly with LE, I got that feeling watching the news conference yesterday.  I even get the feeling they know exactly who he is.  Maybe he IS one of their own and they want to drag it out and spin it any way they can so as not to uncover a corrupt police force.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7920-->
<!--Post: 7956--><!--Time: 1108765528-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7956"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 18, 2005 - 2:25 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Icyou, the FBI is involved. They would also know if it was a corrupt cop and they could never allow WPD to cover it up or aid in a coverup or assist, aid and abet in dragging out the investigation. <BR>BTK is not LE in my opinion.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7956-->
<!--Post: 7979--><!--Time: 1108772232-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7979"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Brown_tornado<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Brown_tornado<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 18, 2005 - 4:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I believe it&#39;s very possible BTK is ex-LE, but there is no cover-up. That part is bullcrap. Too many man hrs., resources, sleepless nights have gone into solving this case.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7979-->
<!--Post: 7981--><!--Time: 1108772351-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7981"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Brown_tornado<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Brown_tornado<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 18, 2005 - 4:19 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->And one other thing...kinda strange that BTK can correctly spell &#34;verification&#34; &#40;Comm. #11 to KSAS&#41;, but can&#39;t spell much easier words...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7981-->
